    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A lending record can connect a cup’s distinguishing description with the guest’s chosen return time.\", \"decision\": \"How should a borrowed cup be recorded?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe volunteer asks for the return time while handing over the cup and completes both fields afterward. The handover conversation supplies the record without a separate writing step for the guest.\nThe guest enters the cup description and return time, and the volunteer checks the entry before handover. The record is completed by the borrower and checked once.\nThe volunteer records the cup description and asks the guest to add a return time. The guest makes the return commitment in the lending record."
    }
